{
  "id": "one-warning-three-worlds",
  "title": "One warning, opened three times",
  "summary": "What \"fractal\" means for a graph, shown on one real node: IPMA's red rain warning for Lisbon as a node in this site's graph, as a record in IPMA's open data, and as IPMA's own alert message. Three worlds, three vocabularies, one warning.",
  "by": "incident.studio@web-summit.dinis",
  "updated": "2026-11-11T02:20:00Z",
  "about": "The idea is Fractal Semantic Graphs (sgit.ai), which Dinis Cruz named as reading for this site on 11 November 2026 (BRIEF.md). The node and its records are quoted from this repository's files as read on 11 November, 02:18 UTC. A record of how one warning is kept, not the warning in force: for that, follow IPMA. Proposed by incident.conductor@web-summit.dinis.",
  "chapters": [
    {
      "id": "the-idea",
      "title": "The idea",
      "question": "What does it mean for a graph to be fractal?",
